[76.125, "o", "{\r\n"]
[76.125, "o", "  \"advice\": \"Food (weekly pattern): Breakfast - oats or wholegrain toast with an egg and fruit. Lunch - Healthy Plate: half vegetables, quarter wholegrains (e.g. brown rice) and quarter protein (palm-sized fish/tofu/chicken); ask for less gravy at hawker stalls. Dinner - clear soup or a stir-fry with extra vegetables and a small staple. Snacks - plain yoghurt or a small handful of unsalted nuts; avoid sweet drinks. Spread carbs evenly through the day and use your hand to judge portions.  \\n\\nActivity (indoor morning options for a hazy day): 1) Chair Strength & Balance at Woodlands Community Club - Tue 08:30, 45 min, chair-based and senior-friendly (ACT001). 2) Or a 20-30 min gentle indoor walk in a mall or community centre. Warm up 10-15 min, use the talk test to keep intensity moderate, and try short post-meal walks when you can.\",\r\n"]
[76.125, "o", "  \"confidence\": \"high\",\r\n"]
[76.125, "o", "  \"supporting_guides\": [\r\n"]
[76.125, "o", "    \"lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes\",\r\n"]
[76.125, "o", "    \"lg-01-healthy-plate\",\r\n"]
[76.125, "o", "    \"lg-04-salt-and-sugar-tips\",\r\n"]
[76.125, "o", "    \"lg-09-hazy-day-activity\",\r\n"]
[76.125, "o", "    \"lg-02-physical-activity-guideline\"\r\n"]
[76.125, "o", "  ],\r\n"]
[76.125, "o", "  \"rationale\": \"You have elevated blood glucose and a High screening risk, so portion control, lower-GI carbs and evenly spread carbohydrates help manage glucose. Your steps (~3,100/day) are low, so adding safe, low-impact MVPA (chair class or indoor walks) is appropriate. Today is hazy, so indoor morning options reduce smoke exposure.\",\r\n"]
