[251.797, "o", "{\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "  \"advice\": \"I'm not a doctor. Food: Follow the Healthy Plate-half vegetables/fruit, quarter wholegrains, quarter protein. Spread carbs across the day and pair carbs with protein to steady blood glucose. Try oatmeal + an egg for breakfast, a small brown-rice lunch with fish or tofu + 2 veg, and a clear soup + lean protein and veg for dinner. Snacks: plain yoghurt, a piece of fruit, or a handful of nuts. Choose water or siew dai/kosong drinks instead of sweet drinks. Activity: It's hazy today, so pick an indoor morning option - try the Morning Chair Strength & Balance class at Woodlands CC (Tue 08:30) for light, senior-friendly strength and balance work, aiming for 20-30 min blocks; if that's not available, do mall walking indoors instead.\",\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "  \"confidence\": \"high\",\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "  \"supporting_guides\": [\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "    \"lg-01-healthy-plate\",\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "    \"lg-05-eating-for-pre-diabetes\",\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "    \"lg-03-nutri-grade\",\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "    \"lg-09-hazy-day-activity\",\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "    \"lg-10-active-after-60\"\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "  ],\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "  \"rationale\": \"You have high screening risk and elevated blood glucose, so steadying carbs and choosing wholegrains/protein helps control glucose. You walk about 3,100 steps (low), so adding a short, indoor morning class or mall walking builds strength and activity safely; hazy conditions make indoor choices safer.\",\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "  \"personalisation_flags\": [\r\n"]
[251.797, "o", "    \"hazy\",\r\n"]
